From c0f08be919d32fc94e64cb19dfb0273f7d6cfea1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P4R4D16M4 <patrickheinzelbecker@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:50:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] V585b: set the vendor PFE netdev parent before
 phy_connect

V585 hardware (blackbox log): firmware load, PE init and pfe_ctrl_init
succeed; pfe_eth_init_one -> phy_connect -> phy_attach_direct oopsed on
the missing netdev parent (same issue as V576 in the port driver).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pfe_ctrl/pfe_eth.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pfe_ctrl/pfe_eth.c b/drivers/pfe_ctrl/pfe_eth.c
index 870c6855a..f271e94ac 100644
--- a/drivers/pfe_ctrl/pfe_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/pfe_ctrl/pfe_eth.c
@@ -3110,6 +3110,9 @@ static int pfe_eth_init_one( struct pfe *pfe, int id )
 
 	priv = netdev_priv(dev);
 	priv->dev = dev;
+	/* ZyxelUntrash V585b: phy_attach_direct() dereferences the netdev's
+	 * parent device (module owner check); without it the probe oopses. */
+	SET_NETDEV_DEV(dev, pfe->dev);
 	priv->id = einfo[id].gem_id;
 	priv->pfe = pfe;
 	/* get gemac tx clock */
-- 
